From 8128d8e20dbf3d117a3c49b87e3d50c2b84343e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Casey Connolly <casey.connolly@linaro.org>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 15:40:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 028/115] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998-google-wahoo: add Pixel 2
 family shared dtsi

Adds the shared devicetree include for Google's "wahoo" msm8998
phone family (Pixel 2 and Pixel 2 XL), covering PMIC, regulator,
pinctrl, and peripheral wiring common to both boards. Per-board files
(msm8998-google-taimen.dts for the Pixel 2 XL, msm8998-google-walleye.dts
for the Pixel 2) include this and override only what differs between
them, primarily the display panel and battery capacity.

GPU voltage is deliberately shot high to stabilize the Adreno A540 at
high frequencies -- a documented, load-bearing workaround, not a
placeholder.

ramoops is scoped here at the board level (rather than SoC-wide in
msm8998.dtsi), since this dtsi is now shared with several more boards
than at this port's 6.0 fork point, and a SoC-wide reservation of a
board-specific carveout address would widen the blast radius for no
functional gain.

Signed-off-by: Casey Connolly <casey.connolly@linaro.org>
Co-developed-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
